# Volt window line and hood — 2026-10-31

The side window base and adjoining shoulder now follow a straight line in the direction marked in the owner's image. The forward cabin is lowered gradually while the overall roof profile is retained. The hood uses a softened square-root fall from the cowl to the nose; the original nose, lamp layout and handling remain in place. Door seams follow the adjusted belt, and the mirrors and window borders remain fitted.

The new actual-mesh checks pass 12/12 in procedural and prepared detailed/simple models. In authoring coordinates the center windscreen foot moves from 0.9994 to 0.9700; the four successive nose-to-cowl hood slopes decrease from 0.333 to 0.246 to 0.202 to 0.155. The exact task-start control fails eight of the new twelve checks, including the window line, cowl height and hood curvature. Retained prepared redesign 150/150, door 100/100, handles 30/30, sport nose 8/8, optics 16/16 and prior nose 10/10 pass. Actual Compatibility Garage/race 58/58 passes; the test logged frame hitches and is not a device performance measurement.

The Volt's prepared meshes, racing shadows, Garage template and picture assets were regenerated. The Garage picture identity includes the Electric mesh asset root so saved images from an older geometry revision are not reused. Identity 5/5 and native picture pipeline 3/3 pass. An isolated six-car persistent-picture seed passes 39/39; a separate restart passes 45/45 with six cache hits, zero renders and matching pixel hashes. The first headless pipeline run was invalid because the test requires a native renderer; the first persistent-picture run lacked its output directory and was rerun successfully with an isolated profile.

Both desktop Compatibility and desktop Mobile produced 18 clean/worn views. The actual [side](evidence/volt-lower-cabin-hood-2026-10-31/final-gl_compatibility/side-opposite-clean.png), [front three-quarter](evidence/volt-lower-cabin-hood-2026-10-31/final-gl_compatibility/front-quarter-high-clean.png), and [race view](evidence/volt-lower-cabin-hood-2026-10-31/final-app/race.png) were inspected. The alignment is a 3D interpretation of the marked line; the owner has not yet reviewed its appearance.

Concurrent vehicle sources were changing during this work. Two initial test processes encountered temporarily absent `hovercraft_kits.gd` and `forklift_kits.gd`; they were stopped and rerun successfully once those files were present. Only the Electric Garage template was regenerated to avoid overwriting other ongoing vehicle work. The shared editor source guard may cause other cars' older Garage templates to rebuild until their own work refreshes them. Godot editor import completed with an unavailable Android build-tools warning; no device or Android build was tested.
